Vulnerability data sources. coverguard does not distribute vulnerability data
with its source code, but it queries or bundles data from the following sources
at the user's direction. If you build or redistribute a snapshot (for example
with "coverguard refresh-vulns"), you must preserve attribution as required by
each source's license:

- OSV.dev (Open Source Vulnerabilities): data licensed under CC-BY-4.0.
  https://osv.dev
- GitHub Advisory Database: data licensed under CC-BY-4.0. Attribution may be
  satisfied by linking to https://github.com/advisories or to the specific
  advisory records used.
- National Vulnerability Database (NVD), NIST: U.S. Government work, public
  domain. https://nvd.nist.gov

